I maintain a small NDMF plugin for VRChat avatars that merges texture atlases. Users add an `AtlasMergeSettings` component (it implements INDMFEditorOnly and has a `bool enableMerge` checkbox) to their avatar root, and my pass runs in the Optimizing phase so it sees the final materials. Several users who also have Avatar Optimizer installed are reporting a Trace and Optimize warning about an unknown component `AtlasMergeSettings` -- mostly the ones who unchecked enableMerge, but sometimes others too. Here's my pass:

```csharp
protected override void Execute(BuildContext ctx)
{
    var settings = ctx.AvatarRootObject.GetComponentInChildren<AtlasMergeSettings>();
    if (settings == null || !settings.enableMerge) return;
    MergeAtlases(ctx, settings);
    Object.DestroyImmediate(settings);
}
```

and in Configure(): `InPhase(BuildPhase.Optimizing).Run(AtlasMergePass.Instance);`. How do I make this compatible with AAO properly?
